<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE precept [
    <!ENTITY date "2026-10-27">
]>

<subsubsection xml:id="subsubsec-square-matrices-taxonomy" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Taxonomy</title>

  <introduction>
    <p>
      Square matrices can be classified into distinct algebraic structures based on their under transposition operators.
    </p>
  </introduction>

  <sidebyside widths="47% 47%" margins="auto">
    <paragraphs xml:id="pars-real-matrix-taxonomy">
      <title>Real-Valued Domain</title>

      <p>
        Transition operations on real-valued square matrices <m>A\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times n}</m> often relies on the
        standard <term>transpose operator</term> <m>A^T</m>.
      </p>

      <p>
        <dl>
          <li>
            <title>Symmetric matrix</title>

            <p>
              Satisfies <m>A=A^T</m>.
            </p>
          </li>

          <li>
            <title>Skew-Symmetric matrix</title>

            <p>
              Satisfies <m>A=-A^T</m>.
            </p>
          </li>
        </dl>
      </p>

    </paragraphs>

    <paragraphs>
      <title>Complex-Valued Domain</title>

      <p>
        sdf
      </p>

    </paragraphs>
  </sidebyside>

</subsubsection>